id: pm-gh1627
title: "GH-1627: bound the entire next response and compact optional TOON sections losslessly"
description: "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1627\n\nReported behavior on published2026.10.28; current-source reproduction and implementation are pending. Preserve the completed predecessor scope when evaluating this report.\n\nFound while orienting an agent session with pm 2026.10.28 on a real tracker (~400 items, 95 ready).\n\nSeverity: medium (paid on every `pm next`, the first command an agent runs to pick work).\n\n`pm next --limit 5` (TOON, default) prints **6,847 bytes / 72 lines** while its own `filters.token_budget` says **640**. `--token-budget` is documented as bounding only \"the ranked ready\" rows; every other section is unbudgeted and the total cost is never reported. Measured bytes by section:\n\n| Section | Bytes |\n| --- | ---: |\n| `blocked[5]` | 1,821 |\n| `containers[5]` | 1,469 |\n| `ready[5]` (the budgeted part) | 1,331 |\n| `decision_needed[3]` | 947 |\n| `recommended` | 397 |\n| `summary` + `filters` + `held_by_others` + four `*_encoding` blocks | ~780 |\n\nThree avoidable costs inside that:\n\n1. **Side sections ignore the budget and the include flags.** `filters` reports `include_decisions: false` and `include_containers: false`, yet `decision_needed[3]` and `containers[5]` are printed in full (15–18 columns each). Agents read the false flags and the printed sections as a contradiction.\n2. **Escaped tag JSON in TOON rows.** 162 `\\\"` sequences, e.g. `\"[\\\"hosted\\\",\\\"tests\\\",\\\"website\\\"]\"`, plus a `json_columns` `*_encoding` block per section. #1603 removed this from `pm context`; `pm next` still has it.\n3. **All-null columns.** 63 `,null` cells (`order`, `deadline`, `assignee`, `parent` are null in almost every row) across the four tables.\n\nExpected (same contract #1401 gave `pm context`): one budget covers the whole response, or the response reports its own total `estimated_tokens` with a per-section breakdown. Side sections collapse to counts plus ids unless explicitly requested (`--include-decisions` / `--include-containers` / `--blocked-limit`). Tags render as TOON arrays, and columns that are null in every row are omitted with an absent-columns receipt. A contract test that `pm next` output stays within `--token-budget` (± a declared envelope) on a large fixture would keep this from regressing.\n"
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: agent-ux,github,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-29T20:35:41.836Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-31T16:19:21.843Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-31T01:51:58.329Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-31T01:51:58.329Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Independently measure the reported large ready-work fixture; Account for every response section and total output cost; Honor explicit side-section includes and preserve resumability; Verify lossless tag encoding null-column receipts and JSON/TOON contracts
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "The TOON codec records omitted null columns by position (null_column_index) instead of repeating the full column list, so the compact table wins for ready and containers and every pm next section list-encodes tags. --token-budget on next is no longer a read-output cost alias, so the universal default ceiling keeps binding the complete response; requesting a selection budget audits the whole envelope (read_output with budget_source default, budget_tokens and estimated_tokens beside truncation.ready_budget) unless an enforced intent receipt already discloses it; filters.token_budget echoes the requested selection ceiling or null. SDK surface snapshot acknowledges NextResult.filters.token_budget (number|null) and PmTableCellEncoding.null_column_index; docs/COMMANDS.md and docs/AGENT_OUTPUT_ENCODINGS.md describe the two budget scopes."
expected_result: Requesting a selection budget on pm next keeps the universal ceiling binding the complete response and discloses its cost; filters.token_budget is null unless requested; tags and omitted null columns stay lossless without changing full SDK data. Default runs carry no receipt and side sections keep their rows; include flags remain dispatch opt-ins.
actual_result: "Measured on the real tracker (229 open, 112 ready): pm next --limit 5 TOON 9,148 -> 8,718 bytes, escaped-quote sequences 182 -> 76 (the remainder is the blockers object column on blocked/containers rows), null cells 30 -> 15, all four sections list-encode tags; --token-budget 640 --json now carries read_output {budget_source: default, budget_tokens: 6000, estimated_tokens: 4119, within_budget: true} and filters.token_budget 640; the default run reports token_budget null and no receipt. Include flags remain dispatch opt-ins, documented as such. Token-budget gate (32 surfaces), context-intent calibration, flag-lexicon/parity/grammar gates and the linked test run pass; negative control fails 3 of 3 new tests before the fix."
