comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T20:35:41.836Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete strict all-status corpus3157 with no omissions or unreadable records, request-specific GH-number and semantic searches, current open/in_progress inventories, and full live predecessor data/comments/history. The predecessor scope is delivered; this report names a distinct boundary. New intake is open and unclaimed. Source report: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1627"
  "2026-10-31T00:44:50.340Z","harness:claude-code","Independent measurement on current source (229 open items, 112 ready) before the fix: pm next --limit 5 TOON 9,148 bytes / 83 lines, 182 escaped-quote sequences, 30 null cells, 4 *_encoding blocks; filters.token_budget reported 640 while nothing enforced it and no read_output receipt was emitted. --token-budget 640 trimmed only recommended+ready (ready_budget estimated 628 within_budget true) and the response stayed 8,879 bytes: the legacy cost alias replaced the universal default ceiling (4000 TOON / 6000 JSON) and resolveBindingReadOutputBudget ignores legacy cost outside context, so the whole-response ceiling was removed rather than applied. The canonical --output-budget 640 omitted the entire result (requested_budget_infeasible; floor of one row per collection + envelope = 1,251 tokens). Codec probe: the compact table candidate lost for ready (1,634 vs 1,592 bytes) and containers (1,805 vs 1,767) only because omitting one all-null column emitted a 15-name column_order list, so those sections fell back to escaped tag JSON; decision_needed and blocked already used list columns."
  "2026-10-31T00:44:50.845Z","harness:claude-code","Fix: (1) PmTableCellEncoding emits null_column_index (original position per omitted null column) instead of the full column_order list; decoders still accept legacy column_order. (2) --token-budget is no longer a read-output cost alias for next, so the universal default ceiling keeps binding the complete response. (3) A requested selection budget always audits the complete envelope: read_output now reports budget_source default, budget_tokens and estimated_tokens beside truncation.ready_budget; an enforced --for intent receipt suppresses the duplicate audit. (4) filters.token_budget is the requested selection ceiling or null. After the fix on the same tracker: TOON default 8,718 bytes (-430), escaped quotes 76 (-106; the remainder is the blockers object column on blocked/containers rows), null cells 15, every section list-encodes tags; pm next --limit 5 --token-budget 640 --json carries read_output {budget_source: default, budget_tokens: 6000, estimated_tokens: 4119, within_budget: true} and filters.token_budget 640; the default run reports token_budget null and no receipt. Gates: token-budget gate (32 surfaces) and context-intent calibration pass; SDK surface snapshot updated with an acknowledgement for NextResult.filters.token_budget (number|null) and the new codec field. Negative control: with the four source files stashed the three new tests fail (expected 640 to be null; null_column_index undefined; legacy order b,a,c)."
  "2026-10-31T08:39:03.580Z","harness:claude-code","Hosted coverage on PR #1637 found two branches only reached through spawned CLI processes (not instrumented): `requiresNextSelectionBudgetAudit` past its command and budget guards, and the null-column restore for columns without a recorded position. Both now have in-process tests: `tests/unit/sdk/read-output-contracts.spec.ts` asserts the audit for `tokenBudget` and the snake-case `token_budget` spelling, no audit without a selection budget, and suppression when an enforced intent receipt already discloses the cost; `tests/unit/sdk/output/table-rows.spec.ts` decodes a partial `null_column_index` and a legacy encoding with neither positions nor `column_order`.\n"
